{
	"cell_id": 6466232524087558650,
	"cells": [
		{
			"cell_id": 6903638965184882636,
			"cell_origin": "client",
			"cell_type": "latex",
			"cells": [
				{
					"cell_id": 8999565782447401964,
					"cell_origin": "client",
					"cell_type": "latex_view",
					"source": "\\package{cdb.core.trigrat}{Canonical simplification of expressions in sines and cosines}\n\nThis package simplifies expressions which are rational functions of sines and\ncosines (and of tan, cot, sec and csc), of any number of angles. Such\nexpressions appear for instance in the components of metrics in polar or\nspheroidal coordinates. Unlike Sympy's generic \\verb|simplify| or\n\\verb|trigsimp|, it brings expressions into a \\emph{canonical form}: expressions\nwhich are equal because of identities such as $\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x = 1$ or the\naddition formulas are mapped to identical results, and an expression which\nvanishes is always recognised as zero. It is also much faster on large\nexpressions.\n\nUse it with \\verb|from cdb.core.trigrat import trigrat|. Importing the package\nalso makes the function available under the name \\verb|\"trigrat\"| to\n\\algo{map_sympy}, and to \\algo{evaluate} through its \\verb|simplify| argument."
				}
			],
			"hidden": true,
			"source": "\\package{cdb.core.trigrat}{Canonical simplification of expressions in sines and cosines}\n\nThis package simplifies expressions which are rational functions of sines and\ncosines (and of tan, cot, sec and csc), of any number of angles. Such\nexpressions appear for instance in the components of metrics in polar or\nspheroidal coordinates. Unlike Sympy's generic \\verb|simplify| or\n\\verb|trigsimp|, it brings expressions into a \\emph{canonical form}: expressions\nwhich are equal because of identities such as $\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x = 1$ or the\naddition formulas are mapped to identical results, and an expression which\nvanishes is always recognised as zero. It is also much faster on large\nexpressions.\n\nUse it with \\verb|from cdb.core.trigrat import trigrat|. Importing the package\nalso makes the function available under the name \\verb|\"trigrat\"| to\n\\algo{map_sympy}, and to \\algo{evaluate} through its \\verb|simplify| argument."
		},
		{
			"cell_id": 8860517885698923525,
			"cell_origin": "client",
			"cell_type": "latex",
			"cells": [
				{
					"cell_id": 6724469250479491219,
					"cell_origin": "client",
					"cell_type": "latex_view",
					"source": "\\algorithm{trigrat(ex: Ex) -> Ex}{Bring sines and cosines into canonical form.}"
				}
			],
			"hidden": true,
			"source": "\\algorithm{trigrat(ex: Ex) -> Ex}{Bring sines and cosines into canonical form.}"
		},
		{
			"cell_id": 8887067849862511141,
			"cell_origin": "client",
			"cell_type": "input",
			"source": "from cdb.utils.develop import inherit_kernel\n\ndef _drop_zero_components(ex):\n    # Remove entries with value zero from all \\components nodes; a node\n    # with no entries left is replaced by zero.\n    while True:\n        found = False\n        for comp in ex[r'\\components']:\n            lst = None\n            for part in comp.args():\n                lst = part\n            empty = True\n            for eq in lst.args():\n                empty = False\n                for j, side in enumerate(eq.args()):\n                    if j == 1 and side.ex() == 0:\n                        found = True\n                if found:\n                    eq.erase()\n                    break\n            if empty:\n                comp.replace(Ex(\"0\"))\n                found = True\n            if found:\n                break\n        if not found:\n            return ex\n\ndef trigrat(ex):\n    \"\"\"Bring all sines and cosines in ex into canonical form.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(ex, Ex):\n        return trigrat_sympy(ex)\n    # Use the caller's kernel, so that its properties (Coordinate, ...)\n    # are seen by map_sympy.\n    kernel = inherit_kernel()\n    if kernel is not None:\n        __cdbkernel__ = kernel\n    map_sympy(ex, \"trigrat\")\n    return _drop_zero_components(ex)"
		},
		{
			"cell_id": 4119880365883813269,
			"cell_origin": "client",
			"cell_type": "latex",
			"cells": [
				{
					"cell_id": 7229623059532238221,
					"cell_origin": "client",
					"cell_type": "latex_view",
					"source": "Acts on all scalar parts of \\verb|ex|, including the values of tensor\ncomponents produced by \\algo{evaluate}. Components which simplify to zero are\nremoved; if no components remain, the components node is replaced by zero. The\nexpression is modified in place and returned. Given a Sympy expression instead\nof a Cadabra expression, it returns the result of \\verb|trigrat_sympy|."
				}
			],
			"hidden": true,
			"source": "Acts on all scalar parts of \\verb|ex|, including the values of tensor\ncomponents produced by \\algo{evaluate}. Components which simplify to zero are\nremoved; if no components remain, the components node is replaced by zero. The\nexpression is modified in place and returned. Given a Sympy expression instead\nof a Cadabra expression, it returns the result of \\verb|trigrat_sympy|."
		},
